\title{orderBookSim: Agent-Based Limit Order Book Simulation for Market Microstructure}
\description{
Simulates a continuous double-auction limit order book with price-time priority matching, driven by configurable populations of trading agents: zero-intelligence order flow in the spirit of Smith, Farmer, Gillemot and Krishnamurthy (2003) \doi{10.1088/1469-7688/3/6/307}, noise traders, inventory-constrained market makers, momentum traders and informed traders who observe a latent fundamental value. Exogenous liquidity shocks can be injected at chosen events. Tools measure time-weighted bid-ask spreads, depth, price impact, resilience after shocks and the stylised facts of returns, and an optional 'shiny' application lets students explore how agent mixes shape liquidity.
}
\section{Getting started}{

Build a book by hand with \code{\link[=lob_new]{lob_new()}} and \code{\link[=lob_submit]{lob_submit()}}, or simulate a
market with \code{\link[=simulate_lob]{simulate_lob()}} and a list of \link{agents}. Measure liquidity with
\code{\link[=summary.lob_sim]{summary.lob_sim()}}, \code{\link[=price_impact]{price_impact()}}, \code{\link[=resilience]{resilience()}} and
\code{\link[=stylized_facts]{stylized_facts()}}, compare agent mixes with \code{\link[=compare_scenarios]{compare_scenarios()}}, and
explore interactively with \code{\link[=run_lob_app]{run_lob_app()}}.
}

